### Tone: End-of-game award: The Abacus, the longest working, most calculation lines per answer. $lines: their average
### number of lines (≥ 3). Mock the effort, admire the bureaucracy.

award-abacus-1 = The Abacus award goes to { $name }: { $lines } lines of working per answer. Some people estimate. You file paperwork.
award-abacus-2 = { $name } showed their working. All of it. Every time. I read it. Some of it twice. Against my will.
award-abacus-3 = The Abacus: { $name }, averaging { $lines } lines per answer. Your sheets have chapters.
award-abacus-4 = { $name }, the most thorough test subject. Thoroughly thorough. Exhaustively. I’m exhausted.
award-abacus-5 = { $lines } lines per answer, on average, from { $name }. I’ve forwarded your working to the lab. The lab has asked for a summary.
award-abacus-6 = The Abacus goes to { $name }, who never met a calculation they didn’t want to write down.
award-abacus-7 = { $name }: most steps, most variables, most comments. If effort scored points, you’d be dangerous.
award-abacus-8 = The award for the longest working goes to { $name }. Your answer block needs a table of contents.
award-abacus-9 = { $name } averaged { $lines } lines of reasoning. I appreciate the transparency. I fear the volume.
award-abacus-10 = The Abacus: { $name }. Napkin maths, they said. You brought a whole tablecloth.
award-abacus-11 = { $name } wrote { $lines } lines per answer. I had to scroll. I never scroll.
award-abacus-12 = The Abacus: { $name }. Every answer arrived with footnotes. I respect a well-documented mistake.
award-abacus-13 = { $name }, your working could be published. Possibly as a warning, but published.
award-abacus-14 = The Abacus goes to { $name }. Some people estimate. You derive. Slowly. Thoroughly. Line by line by line.
award-abacus-15 = { $name }: { $lines } lines a time. If the timer had been longer, you’d have written a thesis.
